      "reason": "Original JCM463 explicitly uses JCM462 with changes only to separately added carbon/electron-acceptor and reducer inputs: sodium lactate is replaced by 20 mM sodium acetate and 30 mM ferric citrate, sodium sulfide is omitted, and 0.5 g/L L-cysteine-HCl is added separately. These late inputs are outside this pre-addition basal material. Its source-listed basal components and quantities therefore share the JCM462 formulation. TOGO M464 riboflavin pointer to M463 resolves to JCM462, whose nested riboflavin preparation lists 2.5 mg riboflavin with 100 ml added water. The 1 ml riboflavin input is a named preparation part; no final volume or derived stock concentration is invented. Both original occurrence and source-version scopes remain explicit; this does not equate the complete growth media."
